# Cold Outreach — example cron schedules (all times Asia/Kolkata / IST)
#
# Install:
#   crontab -e
#   (paste ONE of the schedules below, save, exit)
#
# Verify installed:
#   crontab -l
#
# Disable temporarily (comment out lines):
#   crontab -e   →   put # in front of each line, save
#
# Monitor:
#   tail -f /home/primathon/Documents/p_projet/ColdOutrichAutoEmail/logs/cron-$(date +\%Y-\%m-\%d).log
#
# Emergency stop (kill all queued cron jobs for this script):
#   pkill -f send-batch.sh
#   crontab -r          # nukes the whole crontab — keep a backup
#
# NOTES:
# - Mon-Fri only (`* * 1-5` at the end). Weekends skipped both in cron AND in the wrapper script.
# - The wrapper enforces nvm PATH and weekend skipping defensively.
# - --daily-cap is a HARD ceiling. Even if cron mis-fires, you cannot exceed it.
# - Always include --live in cron entries. Without it, the script does a dry-run and nothing sends.
# - First week: use the WARM-UP schedule below. After day 7, switch to a STEADY-STATE schedule.


# ============================================================
# WARM-UP WEEK (recommended for first 7 days on a fresh account)
# ============================================================
# Conservative ramp. Replace your existing crontab daily — or use
# different --daily-cap values via a single schedule and just adjust.

# Day 1 (10/day, 1 batch — keep it simple, watch for bounces)
# 30 10 * * 1-5 /home/primathon/Documents/p_projet/ColdOutrichAutoEmail/scripts/send-batch.sh --live --cap 10 --daily-cap 10

# Day 2 (15/day, 2 batches)
# 30 10 * * 1-5 /home/primathon/Documents/p_projet/ColdOutrichAutoEmail/scripts/send-batch.sh --live --cap 8 --daily-cap 15
# 30 15 * * 1-5 /home/primathon/Documents/p_projet/ColdOutrichAutoEmail/scripts/send-batch.sh --live --cap 7 --daily-cap 15

# Day 3 (20/day, 2 batches)
# 30 10 * * 1-5 /home/primathon/Documents/p_projet/ColdOutrichAutoEmail/scripts/send-batch.sh --live --cap 10 --daily-cap 20
# 30 15 * * 1-5 /home/primathon/Documents/p_projet/ColdOutrichAutoEmail/scripts/send-batch.sh --live --cap 10 --daily-cap 20


# ============================================================
# STEADY STATE — 30 emails/day, 3 batches (RECOMMENDED for personal Gmail)
# ============================================================
# 10 each at 9:30 AM / 1:00 PM / 5:00 PM IST, Mon–Fri.
# Daily-cap is 30 so even if cron mis-fires you stay safe.
# Prefers T1 (named-person) for the morning batch — highest-value time.

30 9  * * 1-5 /home/primathon/Documents/p_projet/ColdOutrichAutoEmail/scripts/send-batch.sh --live --cap 10 --daily-cap 30 --template T1_NAMED_PERSON
0  13 * * 1-5 /home/primathon/Documents/p_projet/ColdOutrichAutoEmail/scripts/send-batch.sh --live --cap 10 --daily-cap 30
0  17 * * 1-5 /home/primathon/Documents/p_projet/ColdOutrichAutoEmail/scripts/send-batch.sh --live --cap 10 --daily-cap 30


# ============================================================
# AGGRESSIVE — 40 emails/day, 4 batches (use only after 2+ weeks no bounces)
# ============================================================
# Higher cap = higher spam-flag risk on personal Gmail. Watch your reputation.
#
# 30 9  * * 1-5 /home/primathon/Documents/p_projet/ColdOutrichAutoEmail/scripts/send-batch.sh --live --cap 10 --daily-cap 40 --template T1_NAMED_PERSON
# 30 12 * * 1-5 /home/primathon/Documents/p_projet/ColdOutrichAutoEmail/scripts/send-batch.sh --live --cap 10 --daily-cap 40
# 30 15 * * 1-5 /home/primathon/Documents/p_projet/ColdOutrichAutoEmail/scripts/send-batch.sh --live --cap 10 --daily-cap 40
# 30 18 * * 1-5 /home/primathon/Documents/p_projet/ColdOutrichAutoEmail/scripts/send-batch.sh --live --cap 10 --daily-cap 40


# ============================================================
# CRON FIELDS REFERENCE
# ============================================================
#  ┌───── minute (0–59)
#  │ ┌───── hour (0–23, 24-hour clock, local timezone)
#  │ │ ┌───── day of month (1–31)
#  │ │ │ ┌───── month (1–12)
#  │ │ │ │ ┌───── day of week (0=Sun, 1=Mon, …, 7=Sun) — 1-5 means Mon–Fri
#  │ │ │ │ │
#  * * * * *  <command>
